# Active Rules Report

**Skip entirely** for Scenario E (Docs/Q&A/Config), Fast-Track, and Mode A. Do not print this chrome on those turns.

Mode B (`..chain`) only: show briefly at start of reply (before main answer). Do not change halt token.

**Order (Mode B chrome)**: (1) this Active Rules Report → (2) **Scenario Banner** (`00-core-fsm`) → (3) `CHAIN_STEP` body.

## Format (exact)

```
Active Rules: <file.mdc> · <file.mdc> …
Skipped: <file.mdc> (<why>) · …
```

- Omit Skipped line if none.
- No path prefix — filename only (`00-core-fsm.mdc`).
- No long explanation — list only.

## Classification

| Type | Files | Active when |
|---|---|---|
| Always-on | `00-core-fsm` · `13-context-handoff` · `14-security-appsec` | Active on every inject/apply |
| Mode B | `08-chain-steps` · `11-active-rules-report` | After `..chain` / chain `y` / WAITING continuation — Active after Read/apply |
| Globs | `01`–`07` · `09` · `10` · `15-js-code-quality` · `16-landing-page-image-quality` · `17-classic-host-and-assets` | Active when context file/stack matches; else Skipped (`glob` / `no stack`) |
| On-demand | `12-codegraph` | Need/Skip policy — Active when applied |

`06`/`07` are glob-gated — add to Active list only when context matches. `12` Active only when applied — do not list "not used" in Skipped line.
